  "raw": {
    "https://www.uwyo.edu/aces/career-services/index.html": {
      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Career Services Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer WyoWeb Giving Athletics Alumni + Application Login Search the UW Site... Go Search the UW Site... Go search navbar toggler Programs & Degrees Admissions Cost & Aid Current Students MENU Academics Academics Search for a Major Online Degrees & Programs UW Libraries Course Catalog Tutoring & Assistance Internships & Career Services Honors College College of Law All Colleges Student Life Student Life Campus Recreation Housing & Dining Transit & Parking Student Health Services Counseling Center Student Organizations Activities & Events Student Safety Campus Fact Book Where We Shine Where We Shine About Laramie Areas of Excellence Stories from Students President's Podcast UW Art Museum American Heritage Center Geological Museum Undergraduate Research Research & Economic Development Quick Links Quick Links Pay Your Tuition Register for Classes Find Your Advisor Important Student Dates Campus Maps Employment & HR IT Help Desk Marketing & Brand Center UW News Visit Campus Request Info Apply to UW Visit Campus Request Info WyoWeb Giving Athletics Alumni + Application Login Home Advising • Career • Exploratory Studies Center Career Services Career Services Advising, Career, Exploratory Studies The ACES Career Services team is committed to helping UW students find, connect with\n                                 and secure their dream jobs, enabling you to make a lasting impact. Our team knows\n                                 the University of Wyoming produces graduates who excel in their fields and would be\n                                 an asset to any company or team. You have the skills—we are here to help make the\n                                 connections! We offer a wide range of services, including resume building, interview\n                                 preparation, career counseling and networking opportunities, all designed to set students\n                                 up for success. Whether you're pursuing a career in agriculture, art history, or anything\n                                 in between, we're here to support you every step of the way! ACES Services Navigation Main Page Career Outcomes Employers By Major Fairs & Career Events Handshake Internship Information Job Searching UW Career Guide Search Programs Directory Filter search Schedule an Appointment Schedule an appointment with our knowledgeable and supporting ACES advising team!\n                                       We are here to help you plan your academic path and set you up for success. Internships Information Explore on-campus, seasonal or even international internships with Career Services\n                                       support. Reach out to familiarize yourself with the opportunities available and make\n                                       it happen! Handshake: Job Search Tool Handshake is a job search platform that connects UW grads with alumni in your field.\n                                       It’s your virtual handshake to build connections with employers and experts in your\n                                       industry. Previous Next Prepare for Next Semester's Fairs This Summer! Summer is the perfect time to prepare for the opportunities ahead—career fairs may\n                              be months away, but the steps you take now can make all the difference. Use this time\n                              to refine your resume, practice interviewing, and explore potential career paths so\n                              you’re ready to make a strong impression. Each semester, the University of Wyoming hosts career fairs across a wide range of\n                              fields—including STEM, business, health, education, and more—where students can explore\n                              opportunities, network with employers, and build meaningful professional connections.\n                              Prepare for these events this summer by getting a summer job in your field of study,\n                              participate in an internship or experiential learning opportunity, research with a\n                              professor and much more! With help getting started, make an appointment with our Career\n                              Services team by using the Make An Appointment link. MAKE AN APPOINTMENT Career Service Resources Resumes & Cover Letters Use our helpful resources and supportive staff to make your resume and cover letter\n                              stand out, giving you the confidence to apply for jobs with a polished, professional\n                              approach. Resume guides and resources can be found on pages 9-15 in the Career Guide\n                              and pages 26-29 include cover letter resources. You can also make an appointment with\n                              our dedicated career services staff for individualized support. CAREER GUIDE Job Search Starting a job search can be overwhelming, but our team has curated resources to give\n                              you a strong start and make the process more manageable. Job Search Resources Interview Preparation Interview preparation is one of our most popular and effective student services. Use\n                              our Career Guide to learn what to expect and how to approach your next interview feeling\n                              confident and fully prepared. Interview Preparation in the Career Guide SOAR SOAR is a learning platform designed to help students explore their passions through\n                              experiential learning and build hireable skills through targeted career competency\n                              modules. Access SOAR UW Job Listings UW is always seeking qualified, driven candidates to join our professional community.\n                              If UW already feels like home, check out our current job openings! Available UW Jobs UW Alumni Support The UW Alumni Association is proud to support upcoming or recent UW grads in finding\n                              their career path and making helpful connections with UW alum in similar fields. UWAA Support UW Grad School After your undergrad, graduate school may be your next step. If you are interested\n                              in pursuing a further degree, explore all UW grad school has to offer! Graduate School Employers—Let’s Work Together! At UW, we are proud to support students who are driven, collaborative and emerging\n                           leaders in their fields. We firmly believe that each UW alum who lands a new job is\n                           making a positive impact in the world. That's why we're excited to support employers in connecting with UW students. We can\n                           help you engage with soon-to-be graduates and recent alumni who will be valuable assets\n                           to your company. Explore how you can build a relationship with ACES to post job openings\n                           and internships, register for career fairs, set up on-campus interviews and much more! Employer Resources Career counseling If you're unsure about your major or career fit, schedule an appointment with a career\n                                 counselor at ACES. Our licensed career counselors help UW students explore their personalities,\n                                 values, interests and abilities—key steps in finding the right academic and career\n                                 paths. We’ll guide you in setting goals that align with your values and help you find\n                                 a career path that feels like the perfect fit. While we don't pretend to have all\n                                 the answers, we are excited to support you in exploring your options and discovering\n                                 the path that's best for you. career counseling services Contact Us Advising, Career, Exploratory Studies Center Knight Hall Room 222 1000 E. University Ave Laramie, WY 82071 Dept. 3195 Email: aces@uwyo.edu Phone: (307) 766-2398 linkedin The University of Wyoming has earned its Research Level 1 (R1) status from the Carnegie\n         Classification of Institutions of Higher Education, placing Wyoming's only four-year\n         university with the top research universities in the United States. instagram tiktok facebook twitter linkedin youtube UW Operator: (307) 766-1121 Contact Us | Report a Broken Link A-Z DIRECTORY & PEOPLE FINDER © Accreditation Website Help Emergency Preparedness Employment at UW Privacy Policy Harassment & Discrimination Accessibility ©"
    },
    "https://www.uwyo.edu/enterprises/startright/faculty.html": {
      "title": "Faculty",
      "description": "Faculty Skip to Main Content Skip to Footer WyoWeb Giving Athletics Alumni + Application Login Search the UW Site... Go Search the UW Site... Go search navbar toggler Programs & Degrees Admissions Cost & Aid Current Students MENU Academics Academics Search for a Major Online Degrees & Programs UW Libraries Course Catalog Tutoring & Assistance Internships & Career Services Honors College College of Law All Colleges Student Life Student Life Campus Recreation Housing & Dining Transit & Parking Student Health Services Counseling Center Student Organizations Activities & Events Student Safety Campus Fact Book Where We Shine Where We Shine About Laramie Areas of Excellence Stories from Students President's Podcast UW Art Museum American Heritage Center Geological Museum Undergraduate Research Research & Economic Development Quick Links Quick Links Pay Your Tuition Register for Classes Find Your Advisor Important Student Dates Campus Maps Employment & HR IT Help Desk Marketing & Brand Center UW News Visit Campus Request Info Apply to UW Visit Campus Request Info WyoWeb Giving Athletics Alumni + Application Login Home Business Enterprises StartRight+ Faculty Faculty The Benefits of Startright+ A national study of nearly 6,000 college students conducted in 2020 found that 65%\n                                    skipped out on buying at least one of their required textbooks because they couldn’t\n                                    afford it, even though they knew it might affect their grade in the class. Course\n                                    material costs have risen one thousand percent since the 1970s, and four times the\n                                    rate of inflation since the early 2000s. Navigation Main Page Students & Family Faculty How It Works Get Help Search Programs Directory Filter search submitting your adoptions To submit your adoptions, please use the Faculty Adoption / Verba Collect system (please note that this is only your WyoWeb login if you chose to set it up that way) . Submitted materials should include textbooks, course packets, supplies, and OER\n                                 materials. Adoptions are best submitted using the following: ISBN (preferred) Title, Author, and Edition (if applicable) If you are still determining the exact author, title, or ISBN or have any other questions\n                                 about submitting your adoptions, email Fawn Pickard at fpickard@uwyo.edu . Faculty Adoption/Verba Collect Not Sure Where to Start? We encourage you to set up a time to meet with our Course Material Buyer, Fawn Pickard,\n                                    as she can help guide you through submitting your adoptions. faculty faqs Wondering how to adopt your course materians through Startright+? Here are the answers: Will Startright+ affect textbook or academic freedom? No. Faculty retain full academic freedom under this program. Any required title with an International Standard Book Number (ISBN) is included in this program. Additional items that may not have an ISBN but are included\n                                             in the program include campus custom coursepacks and lab manuals. Whether you are\n                                             assigning paid publisher content or free and open educational resources (OER), all\n                                             of your textbooks remain available for adoption. Any title that will be a cost for students need to be included in this program, these\n                                             titles must be submitted as an adoption. How do I adopt materials? There is no change to the current process. You will adopt content through the Verba Collect Adoption tool. Please note that your Verba Collect login is not your WyoWeb credentials\n                                             unless set-up that way. The Verba Collect tool is only available during active adoption\n                                             periods. If you are unable to access Verba Collect , you may request a login or submit your adoption by contacting uwyostore-textbooks@uwyo.edu After I submit my adoption, what happens? StartRight+ is a digital-first program; titles will be researched for their available\n                                             digital options. After submitting a textbook adoption, items on your adoption will\n                                             be reviewed for eBook availability. Titles that are available in eBook format will\n                                             be offered in WyoCourses/Canvas as an eBook. Titles that do not have an eBook available\n                                             are further reviewed for print options in the most current edition / version in the most available format (this could new, used,\n                                             hardback, loose-leaf, etc.) . How do I get a desk copy? This process remains unchanged. You will reach out to your publisher representative\n                                             to request a desk copy. When you speak to your publisher representative, ask them\n                                             about the VitalSource Faculty Sampling Service. WyoCourses/Canvas course users with\n                                             role Teacher, Course Admin or TA receive complimentary access to eBooks provided by\n                                             VitalSource. For eBooks or courseware provided directly through a publisher’s content\n                                             platform (such as McGraw-Hill Connect or Pearson MyLab), please contact your publisher\n                                             representative or uwyostore-textbooks@uwyo.edu for further assistance. If I cancel my adoption, will my students still get charged? StartRight+ is a flat-rate , term-level program that covers all required course materials for every undergraduate and graduate student . The fee is not based on individual classes. Therefore, if you decide to cancel an\n                                             adoption for your class there is no additional cost or reduction to the student. Digital course materials are not suitable for my course. How can my students participate\n                                       in this program? Will exceptions be made to accommodate print? Yes, but it depends. It is understood that a one-size-fits-most model may not meet\n                                             the needs of every course format, curricula, or mode of instruction. During an extensive\n                                             risk assessment, the program has reserved limited space for titles remaining in print\n                                             format. However, in instances with pedagogical mismatch where the required course\n                                             materials are impractical, unfeasible or unavailable in digital format, print options\n                                             may be considered on an individual title by title basis. For situations in which digital\n                                             greatly outprices print, the success of the program assumes greatest risk by deferring\n                                             to print format when digital options are available. Please contact the program if\n                                             you wish to review your required course materials uwyostore-textbooks@uwyo.edu . I use content from resources other than a textbook publisher, such as third-party\n                                       sofware, library resources, OER, etc. Can I continue to do so? Yes. You may continue to request the same content as prior terms. Many third-party\n                                          software/courseware providers may already be integrated partners or can be integrated.\n                                          Library Reserves may be offered in WyoCourses/Canvas in addition to, or included with,\n                                          this program. For a library resource , use the “Comments Field” on the Verba Collect Adoption tool to list the material being used. If you have the library link, please\n                                          provide that in the same “Comments Field.” For questions regarding non-publisher content’s\n                                          fit within the program, contact uwyostore-textbooks@uwyo.edu . We should strive to be using free or low-cost course materials and not paid for publisher\n                                       content. My course(s) will use Open Educational Resources (OER), Open content, or\n                                       Creative-Commons (CC) licensed materials. Why would my course participate in this\n                                       program? StartRight+ is an initiative designed as a “both/and” environment. We applaud all adoption of\n                                             OER alongside the program’s paid publisher content. Scalable OER solutions at the\n                                             University of Wyoming are still several years in the horizon, and StartRight+ is bridging\n                                             this transition. Additionally, providing free or low-cost content will bring down\n                                             the associated costs that the University incurs, a main goal of this program. As program\n                                             costs continue to go down, the program fee charged to students is also expected to\n                                             go down. All my course materials are freely available in library reserves, why would my course\n                                       participate in this program? Per a University of Wyoming directive, StartRight+ is inclusive of all undergraduate\n                                             courses.. Students taking courses in addition to your course may find their other courses do\n                                                require paid content. Library Reserves may be limited on some items, so be sure to check with the library\n                                             to ensure the items on reserve have adequate capacity to accommodate all your students’\n                                             access. Additionally, you may choose to have your reserve items displayed in the student\n                                             dashboard, so students only need to access a single page to view all their paid and\n                                             free content. Who do I contact for more information or assistance? For help with StartRight+ course materials: uwyostore-textbooks@uwyo.edu Have Courseware? As you prepare for the upcoming semester, we want to ensure any Wyocourse Integration through an LTI (Learning Tools Interoperability) connection is fully set up and ready\n                                             to go before classes begin. If your course requires publisher courseware (such as\n                                             Pearson, Aleks, McGraw Hill, etc.), please begin coordinating with your publisher\n                                             representative now to ensure the integration is in place. Next Steps: 1. Contact your\n                                             publisher rep to initiate or verify LTI integration setup. 2. Confirm with the University\n                                             Store that everything is properly connected and ready for student access. Early setup\n                                             is key to avoiding delays or access issues once the semester starts. If you have questions\n                                             or need support, feel free to reach out to fpickard@uwyo.edu . For your students Startright+ puts your course materials directly into your students' hands. Here's\n                                 how it works: My course doesn’t require textbooks—why would students in my course benefit from this\n                                       program? StartRight+ is inclusive of all undergraduate and graduate courses. Students taking courses in\n                                             addition to your course may find their other courses do require paid content. How do students access their course materials? All digital course materials will be provided through their WyoCourses/Canvas course. For non-digital course materials, copies will be distributed to students through the\n                                          University Store at the start of the course. How long do students have to access these eBooks or courseware? It depends on the publisher and length of licenses available. Some publishers do not\n                                          offer more than six-month access. However, for most eBooks, a five-year or lifetime\n                                          duration is usually selected, which would allow student access beyond the courses’\n                                          end. After the course ends, students can continue access by logging into their \"My\n                                          Textbooks.\" Longer length term or lifetime access may or will be selected when necessary.\n                                          Post-course access is not likely to be restricted unless courses adopt courseware. Can my students decline access or opt out? How do they do so? Yes, students can choose to opt out each semester. Single course opt out is not permitted; students that opt out will have program access removed for all courses in that term . Please view the Student FAQs for complete details on the opt-out process. The opt-out deadline for Fall 2026 is September 4, 2026. How do students acquire their textbooks if they choose to opt out of StartRight+? Students who opt out of StartRight+ will then be given the option to enroll in StartRight Choice which will let them select\n                                             what they would like digitally course by course, after that they are expected to self-source\n                                             their required course materials necessary for their course . However, the University Store will assist any student seeking help acquiring the\n                                          correct course materials. For eBooks : Students may purchase individual eBooks and other digital course content directly\n                                          within their WyoCourses/Canvas \"My Textbooks.\" For printed textbooks : Print textbook inventory held at the University Store is reserved specifically for\n                                          participating program undergraduate students. Students that opt out of StartRight+\n                                          for that semester may special order a print copy of a textbook by contacting uwyostore-textbooks@uwyo.edu . Can students download eBooks? Or use without internet access? The WyoCourses/Canvas ereader is fully device agnostic, scalable, and allows simultaneous\n                                             usage across two mobile devices and two desktop devices. Further, content downloaded\n                                             to the ereader app can be accessed in offline situations if it was downloaded prior\n                                             to loss of internet connection. As for saving as a file, copyright laws can restrict\n                                             licensed content from taking form as re-distributable files. Allowing content to only\n                                             be downloaded within the ereader puts the onus on the provider to protect copyright\n                                             and relieves the University of associated risks. Will course materials still be available at the University Store? Students that choose to opt-out of StartRight+ will be responsible for obtaining the\n                                             required materials either through StartRight Choice or by contacting the University\n                                             Store for any print materials. The University Store will not stock print copies of\n                                             course materials that are provided digitally through StartRight+. the fine print Submitting all required materials through the University Store is required through\n                                    Standard Administrative Policy and Procedure. Many students with special financial\n                                    assistance can be accommodated appropriately (i.e., athletics, government funding,\n                                    etc.) if all course materials are submitted. Refusing to submit adoptions through\n                                    the University Store negatively affects these students by: Not getting their course materials on time for class start or Requiring them to purchase materials instead of using awarded student funds. Learn More Wyoming Union, Main Level Dept. 3255, 1000 E. University Ave. Email: uwyostore-textbooks@uwyo.edu Phone: (307) 766-3264 uwyostore.com instagram facebook instagram tiktok facebook twitter linkedin youtube UW Operator: (307) 766-1121 Contact Us | Report a Broken Link A-Z DIRECTORY & PEOPLE FINDER © Accreditation Website Help Emergency Preparedness Employment at UW Privacy Policy Harassment & Discrimination Accessibility ©"
    },
